  "ai_stories": [
    {
      "id": "nvidia",
      "paragraph": "Nvidia designs chips that help computers train AI models and run them after training. When a model answers a question, for example, chips do the calculations needed to produce the reply. On November 12, Nvidia announced that Jensen Huang resigned as president, chief executive and board director, effective immediately. Colette Kress, the company’s finance chief, took over as interim chief executive, meaning she leads the company while the board searches for a permanent successor. The board’s choice is still open, and the announcement leaves Nvidia’s future strategy under its next leader unclear.",
      "headline": "Nvidia names an interim CEO",
      "sources": [
        "https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-Announces-CEO-Transition/default.aspx",
        "https://apnews.com/article/jensen-haung-china-spy-nvidia-aritificial-intelligence-f9ac67fed10c86c1ed1ad1f41dd921a5"
      ],
      "edit": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cisco",
      "paragraph": "When several computers work together on an AI task, they need to pass information between them. For example, one machine may need another machine’s results before it can finish its own calculations. Cisco sells equipment that helps computers in data centres exchange that information. On November 12, Cisco reported first quarter revenue of US$18.5 billion, up 24% from a year earlier. Reuters cited strong demand for AI networking and cybersecurity equipment. Cisco also raised its forecast for fiscal 2027 revenue to US$74.8 billion to US$75.8 billion from US$72.2 billion to US$73.4 billion. The full year result remains uncertain.",
      "headline": "Cisco raises its full-year revenue forecast",
      "sources": [
        "https://newsroom.cisco.com/c/r/newsroom/en/us/a/y2026/m11/cisco-reports-first-quarter-earnings.html",
